{"c":[{"id":"b51bc99b3aa533a8","sum":"B14: load-proof tests fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (find exposed ones with a wall clock jumping 1 s per read); a name field is withheld only on namesCut, since counting names prose mentions blanked Full name on Messages sets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100918Z-d51f417a758957f9","text":"Tests whose answers must not depend on CPU load fix the generator's budget clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (candidates.ts); find exposed tests by making the wall clock jump 1 s per read and rerunning the suite (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-90979468cad825fe","text":"Names are a fill kind (kinds.ts NAME_TERM): a field that takes a name is withheld only when namesCut (name-like lines or a contact line's names kept out, a partway cap/clock stop, cutAll); counting names that prose mentions blanked Full name on every Messages set (B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d0f5d3ab6d535ae7","sum":"B14: a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase); before a live replay, run a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev to see withholding and wrong fills for free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100919Z-9bbdea6cd359a808","text":"A stopped taskProgress must carry stopReason: executor progress() refuses 'stopped' at type level and stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase so the exported JSON Schema states the rule (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-aefa98c201821a3a","text":"Before a live replay, copy live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev (gold if offered, else a name-like decoy) to see withholding and wrong fills for free; B14's copy is ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b14/oracle/oracle-replay.ts.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
